id: pm-l5bc03
title: "Exact-head review hardening: terminator-safe create mode, complete item ID conflict parsing, and public changelog integrity"
description: "Resolve all four actionable findings from the exact-head CodeRabbit review at 55404c0b7 in one feedback-round hardening tranche: stop create-mode option parsing at the argument terminator, reject every ambiguous item identifier form, remove internal process notes from the public generated changelog through canonical PM metadata, and preserve honest generator-gate evidence."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:cli","area:release","area:sdk",changelog-exclude,pr-957,regression,review-hardening
created_at: "2026-08-09T23:34:03.288Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T01:21:24.823Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-10T01:21:24.347Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-10T01:21:24.347Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Create-mode help policy ignores operands after -- while preserving both supported option forms before it; Item addressing rejects duplicate named IDs and positional-plus-named IDs regardless of intervening flags; Generated public changelog contains user-facing capability changes only and pm-changelog verification passes; Focused, full, coverage, static, and manual acceptance gates pass before closure"
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: "Made create-mode help parsing terminator-aware; made item-address normalization consume declared flag arity across the complete pre-terminator stream, reject every mixed-ID ambiguity, preserve valid trailing operands, and copy value metadata; made command suggestion ties locale-independent; documented recovery insertion before --; retained canonical changelog exclusion and waiver-specific PM evidence."
expected_result: "Every item-addressed invocation resolves one unambiguous ID through declared flag arity, create-mode policy stops at --, and generated public notes exclude internal review records."
actual_result: "Focused SDK tests pass; full repository suite passes 466 files and 7,111 tests; exact coverage is 50,834/50,834 statements, 37,194/37,194 branches, 10,438/10,438 functions, and 49,180/49,180 lines; static quality and isolated manual acceptance remain green."
